  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "con-atau",
  "connector": "atau",
  "gloss": "or",
  "title": "atau — or",
  "pattern": "A atau B? · … atau tidak?",
  "explanation": "atau offers a choice between two things or two actions: teh atau kopi?, hari ini atau besok? Staff ask this way all the time, so listen for it: Pakai sambal atau tidak? — With chilli sauce or without? Putting atau tidak at the end (casual atau nggak, or just nggak) turns any question into or not?: Mau ikut atau nggak? — Do you want to come or not?",
  "natural": "Choices, polite or casual. In casual speech people often say apa instead of atau in a choice question: Mau teh apa kopi?",
  "stiff": "Ending your own question with atau tidak? can sound pushy, like or not? in English. With someone you don't know, just ask with a rising tone: Bapak mau ikut?",
